  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "People go by a short everyday first name (roepnaam), often different from the formal names on their passport (Johannes becomes Jan or Hans). Family names often carry a lower-case prefix (tussenvoegsel) such as van, de, van der or van den: Lotte van der Berg, but Mevrouw Van der Berg when the first name is dropped, and it is sorted under B. Children take the father's or mother's family name, chosen by the parents. Dutch people of Surinamese, Antillean, Moroccan, Turkish and Indonesian heritage are part of every big city, and the tech hubs draw many internationals.",
